<!-- =====================================
                     INTRODUCTION
                ====================================== -->
<section class="chapter" id="introduction">
<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>
                        An operating system manages the resources
                        required by computer programs, including
                        the CPU, memory, storage, files, and
                        hardware devices.
                    </p>
<p>
                        Modern computers execute multiple processes
                        simultaneously. This multitasking capability
                        allows programs to share resources, but it
                        can also produce conflicts.
                    </p>
<p>
                        A deadlock occurs when processes cannot
                        continue because each is waiting for
                        resources held by another process.
                    </p>
<p>
                        Proper resource allocation and deadlock
                        management help maintain computer
                        performance, reliability, and stability.
                    </p>
</section>
